            <ArticleTitle>MR imaging of pseudoaneurysms in aortocoronary bypass graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>426-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysm formation may complicate aortocoronary saphenous vein bypass grafts. Because of multiplanar imaging capabilities and the potential for flow evaluation, magnetic resonance (MR) is useful as a noninvasive diagnostic technique. Two cases of pseudoaneurysm formation were evaluated by MR and demonstrate the clinical value of this modality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
